d  their blood called kaiju blue is an  ammonia-based fluid it is highly  corrosive highly toxic to humans and  rapidly vaporizes in air following the  death of the kaiju  so should they be killed in battle their  bodies are triggered to self-destruct  immediately the blood or the flute of a  kaiju is as i said before ammonia base  the kaiju blue has the potential to  poison the air and the surroundings  around it making the land uninhabitable  kaiju's blood is very corrosive  corroding everything in its path this  makes it particularly difficult to  collect samples for testing and  experimentation in a safe manner  although later  when it was successful to collect them  the kaiju blue was utilized and modified  into rocket fuel and can even be used as  explosives and for power generation  so before we go on to the life cycle of  this kaiju let's talk about their  categorization or classification kaiju  have been categorized into different  categories  with categories 1 and 2 representing the  weakest of them while 3 to 5 are the  strongest with a new category 6 seen in  the season 2 of the black classification  is based on size toxicity and radiation  levels given off by their bodies kaiju  are highly aggressive creatures  especially in combat they can combine  with the help of rippers as in the case  of the mega kaiju when two category  fours and one category five kaiju merged  to form this possibly category 6 1 but  then the first confirmed category 6  kaiju is the breacher from season 2 of  the black which seemed to be strong but  then still weaker than slaton or the  mega kaiju even though it is one  category above them  okay so now let's get to the  reproduction and the life cycle of these  kaiju they are stated to be created and  not born their tissue is cloned from a  single strand of tri-helix dna and the  precursors assemble these creatures by  connecting the clone pieces all kaijus  share the same genotype but have widely  varying phenotypes this results 